content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-24020",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 92 °C and rising. HF-300 bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface, and the applicable limits are normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. The reading is 22 °C above the upper normal value, 12 °C above the alarm limit and 2 °C above the trip limit. The 90 °C trip limit governs the decision to stop the pump; because the reading is also above the 80 °C alarm limit, a priority-1 work order is required within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Using Figure 3, the reported vibration of 4.0 mm/s falls within Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below the 4.5 mm/s RMS Zone C restricted-operation boundary and the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone D damage-likely boundary, so this value alone does not trigger the highest-vibration-zone stop and reliability-engineer notification rule. This vibration classification does not permit continued operation while the bearing temperature is above its trip limit. Figure 3 applies to RMS vibration velocity measured on bearing housings, so the report's measurement basis must be confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The noisy bearing meets the manual's replacement trigger even without separate confirmation of wear: section 5.3 requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature. This bearing has both reported noise and excessive temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The condition-monitoring method requires vibration velocity to be measured on both bearing housings and the highest reading to be classified. Only one vibration value is reported, so 4.0 mm/s cannot yet be confirmed as the highest reading for the machine.",
      "citations": [
        "C06"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear or damage is the leading candidate: it is a documented cause of both high bearing temperature and high vibration, and the reported noise and temperature already require replacement of the bearing pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment is the next candidate because the troubleshooting table lists it as a cause of both high bearing temperature and high vibration. Check alignment and perform laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented cause of high bearing temperature. Check the grease quantity during the investigation; the evidence does not provide the required quantity.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation are less specific alternative contributors to vibration. Inspect the impeller and check NPSH; the report contains no impeller or NPSH findings to confirm either cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-110 immediately and keep it out of service: the reported 92 °C bearing-housing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's 90 °C trip limit. Do not rely on the Zone B vibration classification to justify continued running.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Execute this as a P1 work order within the shift because the bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's 80 °C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal work, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; isolate and drain the pump; drain and vent before obtaining the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. Remove the back pull-out assembly as required for access; its documented mass is 68 kg, which exceeds the 25 kg lifting-control threshold. The back pull-out design allows the rotating assembly to be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the documented causes before reassembly: check grease quantity, inspect both bearings and the impeller, check NPSH, and assess alignment. Record the findings so the replacement does not leave an underlying misalignment, lubrication, impeller or cavitation problem uncorrected.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end bearing HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 (6310-C3). Replacement is mandatory under section 5.3 because one bearing is noisy and overtemperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If mechanical-seal removal or replacement is included in the accepted disassembly scope, follow section 5.2: remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, inspect the sleeve for scoring, and fit the new seal and a new casing gasket when replacing the seal. For this serial, use HF3-450B rather than HF3-450; it is pre-set and needs no sleeve setting measurement. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, use the applicable manual torques with lightly oiled threads: M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm; if removed, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; and, if casing bolts are disturbed, M16 casing bolts 210 Nm. Replace casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened. If an HF3-450B seal is fitted, tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Achieve parallel offset no greater than 0.05 mm and angular misalignment no greater than 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before returning the pump to service, restore the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and ensure the pump is never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "During post-repair verification, recheck bearing-housing surface temperature against the 70 °C normal, 80 °C alarm and 90 °C trip values. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3; continue weekly monitoring thereafter. If any reading is classified in Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; required, and to be replaced as a pair with HF3-510 because the drive-end bearing is noisy and overtemperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; required as the other bearing of the mandated replacement pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; conditional on opening the casing or performing mechanical-seal replacement. Replace whenever the casing is opened, and fit a new gasket during seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; conditional on seal replacement being included in the work scope. This is the required replacement for HF3-450 on serial HF3-24020, with a 30 Nm gland-nut torque. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional on inspection during seal work. Replace if sleeve scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediate temperature control: stop the pump because 92 °C exceeds the manufacturer's 90 °C trip limit. Separately, its exceedance of the 80 °C alarm limit requires this P1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolation control for work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting control: the 68 kg back pull-out assembly requires lifting equipment and exceeds 25 kg, so use certified lifting equipment and a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the pump is on a chemically dosed line, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dry-running control: maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The highest-severity vibration rule is not triggered by a valid 4.0 mm/s RMS Zone B reading. If subsequent measurements reach Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement, pair: standard labour allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician; applicable after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement: standard allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, to be added only if seal replacement is included in the approved scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, and manual Table 5 gives M10 seal gland nuts a torque of 25 Nm. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead prohibits HF3-450 and specifies pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B with a 30 Nm gland torque for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-110 is serial HF3-24020, so the bulletin applies to this asset. If seal work is performed, use HF3-450B and 30 Nm; do not fit HF3-450 or use 25 Nm. The bulletin also requires sleeve replacement when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. This decision does not alter the other documented Table 5 torques.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 4.0 mm/s vibration an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what is the vibration reading on the other housing? These details are required to apply Figure 3 and classify the highest reading as the manual directs [C06, C07].",
    "What grease type and grease quantity are specified for these bearings, and how much grease is currently present? Over-greasing must be checked, but no lubrication specification or quantity is supplied in the evidence [C09].",
    "Does bearing access require removal of the impeller or mechanical seal, or opening of the casing? The evidence does not provide a bearing-specific disassembly procedure; this determines whether the conditional seal, sleeve and gasket parts and the additional seal-replacement labour are needed [C10, C12].",
    "If the seal and sleeve are withdrawn, what is the measured sleeve-scoring depth? Sleeve HF3-455 is required only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth [C10, C13].",
    "What are the inspected bearing condition, impeller condition, alignment readings and NPSH results? The report does not establish which of the documented causes is responsible [C09].",
    "Is P-110 installed on a chemically dosed line? This determines whether chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory [C15]."
  ]
}
